From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:41:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda + cuda/exl3: decode kernels and expert decode
 loads behind switches, default off (MiaAI-Lab recipe patches 0016, 0019,
 0031, 0043, 0047)

Mia's decode-window kernels, ported from her GLM-5.3-Flash recipe @ 1576746 onto the AFD 0.6.5 branch. Each sits
behind its own switch, Mia's env name where she has one, and every switch is off unless set: with none set, every
launch and every Python call is the one before.

Attention node:
- TF_GLM_Q4_TILE=table|0-15 (0016, 0019): decode rows (<= 16) of a Q4 matmul on another qmm_kernel tile config
  (qmm_cfg, configs 0-15 incl. 0019's 32-column blocks), her per-shape table as it is; ported onto 0.6.5's qmm.cu.
- TF_GLM_KDA_WIDE_ROWS=N (0016): windows of N rows or more take the wide KDA chain (her 1), with its scratch
  reserved before capture.
- TF_GLM_HC_DEC=1 (0019): decode rows' hyper-connection mixing dots in the new hc.cu (48 blocks a row), its
  _hc_partial's bits; new extension tensorfold_glm_hc_v2 (prebuild it with the others).
- TF_GLM_LATENT_STAGES=1-3 (0019): the latent chunk programs' pipeline depth (her 3).
- TF_GLM_DECODE_SELECT=1 (0031, 0043; her tree runs them unconditionally): decode windows score each row once over
  the pools it can see and select over its visible columns only; the same tokens (Triton interpreter: equal to the
  base and to her tree on 8 cases).

Expert nodes (the universal EXL3 kernel; 4-bit mcg at GLM's tile settings):
- TF_GLM_EXL3_DEC=1, TF_GLM_EXL3_FUSE=0|1, TF_GLM_EXL3_XROW (0016): decode windows through her dec_kernel adapted
  onto the universal grouping, the down projection's epilogue fused (FUSE 1), one rotated input a row (XROW).
- TF_GLM_EXL3_LOADS=nc|nc2|nc4 (0047; her recipe's config sets nc, and it turns the decode kernel on here unless
  TF_GLM_EXL3_DEC=0): 16-byte ld.global.nc trellis loads 1, 2 or 4 k steps ahead, which she adapted from
  jayleaton/glm53-tensorfold-spark patch 0580 (Apache-2.0).

Not ported: 0019's TF_GLM_COMBINE_SY (the AFD attention node sums the shared row in hc_post; the line it changes runs
only without AFD), her TF_GLM_EXL3_FUSE 2/3 (measured slower in her notes). Extensions renamed tensorfold_qmm_v6 and
tensorfold_exl3_experts_v3 (new ops).

Tests: tests/test_glm_decode_kernels.py (CPU: switches, refusals, routing with recording fakes, the load ring model,
the selection through the Triton interpreter) and tests/cuda/test_glm_decode_kernels.py (GPU: each kernel against the
unpatched one, byte for byte; skipped without CUDA).

Credit: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("GLM decode kernels") and the ported units' comments name MiaAI-Lab, the patches and,
for 0047's loads, Jay Leaton's patch.

Co-authored-by: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (planning and execution), via Hermes

