+## GLM decode kernels
+
+The decode-window kernels and switches of `cuda/kernels/qmm.{cu,cpp,py}` (`qmm_cfg`, `dispatch_cfg`, the 32-column
+weight load) with `families/glm5_next/cuda/qmm.py` (`DEC_TILES`, `dec_tile`: `TF_GLM_Q4_TILE`), `kda.py` and
+`decode.py` (`TF_GLM_KDA_WIDE_ROWS`, the wide scratch reserved before capture), `hc.cu` / `hc.cpp` with `glue.py`
+(`hc_dec`, `_hc_ext`: `TF_GLM_HC_DEC`), `latent.py` (`chunk_stages`: `TF_GLM_LATENT_STAGES`), `sparse.py`
+(`_scores_rows`, `ROW_SCORE_G`, `_visible_bound`, `_tokens`, `_select_split`'s `VIS` / `TOKS`, `select_split`'s `pos`,
+`_top_pools_visible`, `_select_decode`: `TF_GLM_DECODE_SELECT`) and `cuda/exl3/experts.{cu,cpp,py}` with
+`exl3_generic.py` (`dec_kernel`, `ldg_nc_v4`, `exl3x_dec_cuda`, `dec_ready`, `nc_aligned`, `_dec_routed`, `dec_loads`,
+`dec_switches`: `TF_GLM_EXL3_DEC`, `TF_GLM_EXL3_FUSE`, `TF_GLM_EXL3_XROW`, `TF_GLM_EXL3_LOADS`) are ported from
+MiaAI-Lab's
+[GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Spark recipe](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/tree/1576746)
+patches 0016-glm-decode-kernels, 0019-glm-decode-kernels2, 0031-glm-decode-index-regs, 0043-glm-visible-pools and
+0047-glm-exl3-decode-loads (with the decode-row routing of 0029 and the `_tokens` kernel of 0009 that 0043's code
+uses), Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 MiaAI-Lab (see [the license text](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)). `hc.cu` and
+`hc.cpp` are her files with a credit line; her Triton and Python units are taken as they are, with the switch reads
+and ruff's imports changed. The tile configs, `qmm_cfg` and the 32-column load are her code on this tree's newer
+`qmm.cu` (its `LaneTile` launch). The EXL3 decode kernel is an adaptation of her `dec_kernel`, written for GLM's
+dedicated EXL3 kernel, onto the universal kernel's grouping (an item is an expert's 16-member tile with the expert's
+own trellis pointer; GLM's 4-bit mcg layers at its tile settings only), not a copy; her fused gate/up epilogue
+(`TF_GLM_EXL3_FUSE` 2 / 3, measured slower in her notes) is not ported. 0047's 16-byte non-coherent trellis loads are,
+as her recipe credits them, adapted from patch 0580 of
+[jayleaton/glm53-tensorfold-spark](https://github.com/jayleaton/glm53-tensorfold-spark) (`exl3_ld.cu`'s `ld_kernel`,
+`LD_NC`), Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 Jay Leaton. Every switch here is off unless set (her recipe turns them
+on); with none set, every launch is the one before the port.
